# Open Design — env var reference
#
# These are environment variables the daemon reads on startup. Copy what you
# need to your shell profile (~/.zshrc / ~/.bashrc), export them before
# running `pnpm tools-dev`, or copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored)
# and source it before launching the daemon. The daemon itself does NOT load
# .env files — vars must be present in process.env at startup.

# --- Cloud (multi-user collaboration; opt-in per project) ---

# Supabase project URL. From https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/<ref>/settings/api
# Leave empty to disable cloud features; daemon will hide cloud UI surface.
OD_CLOUD_URL=

# Supabase publishable (anon) key. Same source as above. This is safe to ship
# in client code — RLS in Postgres enforces per-row authorization. Do NOT use
# the service_role key here.
OD_CLOUD_ANON_KEY=

# Optional: explicit landing-page URL used in invitation emails. Defaults to
# the Cloudflare Pages site we deploy. Override for local testing.
# OD_CLOUD_INVITE_LANDING_URL=https://invite.yourdomain.com

# --- Local runtime (existing) ---

# Custom data directory. Default: <projectRoot>/.od
# OD_DATA_DIR=/custom/path

# Web/daemon ports (set by tools-dev when running through it):
# OD_PORT=17456
# OD_WEB_PORT=17573
